@startuml
title SDD v2 — Proposed same-origin extension authentication relay (D51 review)
hide footbox
autonumber

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #EAF2FB
  BorderColor #1F5A99
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #333333
  LifeLineBorderColor #777777
  GroupBorderColor #1F5A99
  GroupHeaderFontColor #1F5A99
}

actor Analyst
boundary "Extension Popup" as Popup
participant "Offscreen Tab\nCapture" as Capture
participant "Content Script\n(app origin only)" as Content
boundary "Authenticated Relay Page\n/live/extension" as Page
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Live Session\nService" as Live

Analyst -> Page: open relay page after normal sign-in
activate Page
Page -> Page: create one-use pairing nonce
Analyst -> Popup: Start active-tab analysis
activate Popup
Popup -> Capture: begin tabCapture after user action
activate Capture
Popup -> Content: pair(nonce, exact page window)
activate Content
Content -> Page: establish page-scoped MessageChannel
Page -> Gateway: WSS /api/live (first-party D47 cookie)
activate Gateway
Gateway -> Live: authorize handshake
activate Live
Live --> Page: accepted | refused

loop while paired and running
  Capture -> Content: mono PCM chunk
  Content -> Page: validated chunk over MessageChannel
  Page -> Live: WebSocket audio frame
  Live --> Page: running evidence / verdict
  Page --> Content: visible state
  Content --> Popup: visible listening/result state
end

alt Stop, navigation, tab close, sign-out or failure
  Page -> Live: close live session
  Page -> Content: close channel; invalidate nonce
  Content -> Capture: stop capture
end
deactivate Live
deactivate Gateway
deactivate Content
deactivate Capture
deactivate Popup
deactivate Page

note over Popup,Live
  The extension receives no cookie, bearer token or reusable API credential.
  An unpaired extension, non-app origin or replayed nonce is refused.
end note

legend bottom
  Proposed design: team SDD/security approval is required before implementation
  The same-origin page owns the authenticated WebSocket; the extension only relays captured audio
endlegend
@enduml
